  "text": "Barrows Basic\n\n​\nIntroduction\nThe Barrows Brothers  were originally composed of six wights, two more members were added after completing the Ritual of the Mahjarrat and Kindred Spirits quests.\n​\n⬥ This guides aims to get you started on doing Barrows runs, and will focus on the original six brothers.\n‎ ‎ ‎ ‎• It will be assumed that you're using Magic  and the entry-level preset.\n⬥ War's Retreat is used for easy access to the Barrows Brothers \n‎ ‎ ‎ ‎• War's Retreat Teleport  is unlocked via getting 10 boss kills (any boss).\n⬥ Using High Contrast Mode lets you see which door is clickable when in the tunnels.\n‎ ‎ ‎ ‎• Right-click the World Map to toggle it on.\n​\nPresets and Relics\n⬥ Magic - Mid-level \n⬥ Magic - Entry-level \n\n⬥ The mid-level preset and example video can be used as a reference if you're interested in killing Akrisae and Linza.\n​\nUseful Unlocks\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n⬥ The following allow you to increase the efficiency of your runs:\n    • Although useful, they are not mandatory.\n\nItems\n⬥ Salve amulet (e) \n    • Increases damage and accuracy by 20% when fighting undead monsters.\n⬥ Ghost hunter equipment \n    • Increases damage done against ghosts related creatures by 10% when three or more pieces are worn.\n⬥ Powerburst of acceleration \n    • Surge  and Dive  will increase the speed of your runs.\nOther\n⬥ Luck enhancers \n    • Increases chances at barrows equipment  and amulet of the forsaken \n    • You only need tier 2 luck.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n​\nMechanics\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThe Brothers\n\n⬥ As this is an older encounter, there aren't many mechanics to be wary of.\n    • Each brother has a mechanic, which can mostly be ignored.\n        ⬩ Dharok increases his damage dealt, the lower his life points get.\n    • Being underground will periodically drain your prayer points.\n    • The catacombs are a maze, with a simple puzzle at the end.\n\nThe Catacombs\n⬥ Searching one of the sarcophagi will place you in a random corner of the catacombs.\n    • This sarcophagus is random, and normally reserved for last.\n⬥ The catacombs are composed of a series of tunnels, in the shape of a 3x3 grid, with a treasure room in the center.\n    • The path to the center is randomly generated.\n    • Using High Contrast Mode makes finding the correct path easier.\n⬥ The door leading to the center of the catacombs will have one of four, simple puzzles, which always have the same solution.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n​\nThe Fight\nOrder the Brothers Should be Killed\nDharok → Ahrim → Karil → Guthan → Torag → Verac\n⬥ You can use protection prayers to mitigate damage.\n‎ ‎ ‎ ‎ ‎ ‎ ‎ ‎⬩ Protect from Melee  on Dharok, Guthan, Torag, and Verac.\n‎ ‎ ‎ ‎ ‎ ‎ ‎ ‎⬩ Protect from Magic  on Ahrim.\n‎ ‎ ‎ ‎ ‎ ‎ ‎ ‎⬩ Protect from Ranged  on Karil.\n⬥ Try to make good use of Surge  and Dive \n​\nRotations\n⬥  /  →  →  →  → improv\n‎ ‎ ‎ ‎• Alternate starts between Wild Magic  and Asphyxiate \n​\nExample Kills\n⬥ Mid-level\n⬥ Entry-level\n\n\n​\n      \n    ",
  "normalizedText": "Barrows Basic ​ Introduction The Barrows Brothers were originally composed of six wights, two more members were added after completing the Ritual of the Mahjarrat and Kindred Spirits quests. ​ ⬥ This guides aims to get you started on doing Barrows runs, and will focus on the original six brothers. ‎ ‎ ‎ ‎• It will be assumed that you're using Magic and the entry-level preset. ⬥ War's Retreat is used for easy access to the Barrows Brothers ‎ ‎ ‎ ‎• War's Retreat Teleport is unlocked via getting 10 boss kills (any boss). ⬥ Using High Contrast Mode lets you see which door is clickable when in the tunnels. ‎ ‎ ‎ ‎• Right-click the World Map to toggle it on. ​ Presets and Relics ⬥ Magic - Mid-level ⬥ Magic - Entry-level ⬥ The mid-level preset and example video can be used as a reference if you're interested in killing Akrisae and Linza. ​ Useful Unlocks ⬥ The following allow you to increase the efficiency of your runs: • Although useful, they are not mandatory. Items ⬥ Salve amulet (e) • Increases damage and accuracy by 20% when fighting undead monsters. ⬥ Ghost hunter equipment • Increases damage done against ghosts related creatures by 10% when three or more pieces are worn. ⬥ Powerburst of acceleration • Surge and Dive will increase the speed of your runs. Other ⬥ Luck enhancers • Increases chances at barrows equipment and amulet of the forsaken • You only need tier 2 luck. ​ Mechanics The Brothers ⬥ As this is an older encounter, there aren't many mechanics to be wary of. • Each brother has a mechanic, which can mostly be ignored. ⬩ Dharok increases his damage dealt, the lower his life points get. • Being underground will periodically drain your prayer points. • The catacombs are a maze, with a simple puzzle at the end. The Catacombs ⬥ Searching one of the sarcophagi will place you in a random corner of the catacombs. • This sarcophagus is random, and normally reserved for last. ⬥ The catacombs are composed of a series of tunnels, in the shape of a 3x3 grid, with a treasure room in the center. • The path to the center is randomly generated. • Using High Contrast Mode makes finding the correct path easier. ⬥ The door leading to the center of the catacombs will have one of four, simple puzzles, which always have the same solution. ​ The Fight Order the Brothers Should be Killed Dharok → Ahrim → Karil → Guthan → Torag → Verac ⬥ You can use protection prayers to mitigate damage. ‎ ‎ ‎ ‎ ‎ ‎ ‎ ‎⬩ Protect from Melee on Dharok, Guthan, Torag, and Verac. ‎ ‎ ‎ ‎ ‎ ‎ ‎ ‎⬩ Protect from Magic on Ahrim. ‎ ‎ ‎ ‎ ‎ ‎ ‎ ‎⬩ Protect from Ranged on Karil. ⬥ Try to make good use of Surge and Dive ​ Rotations ⬥ / → → → → improv ‎ ‎ ‎ ‎• Alternate starts between Wild Magic and Asphyxiate ​ Example Kills ⬥ Mid-level ⬥ Entry-level ​",
